# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [6.0.0] - 2026-10-28

### Changed

- **Breaking:** Requires `@schorts/shared-kernel` 11.x.
- **Breaking:** Requires Node.js 22 or later (declared in `engines`), as `firebase-admin` 14 does.
- The ES module build is real ES modules. Before, `dist/esm` held CommonJS, so ES module apps loaded a second copy of the kernel: entity dates were not stored as `Timestamp`s, geohashes were not written, and reads failed with `EntityNotRegistered`.
- README examples rewritten for Shared Kernel 11; they are type-checked with the AI docs.
- The package ships the LGPL `LICENSE` and the GPL `COPYING` it references.
- Updated `firebase-admin` to 14.x.
- `GEO_RADIUS` filters accept every value shape the Shared Kernel defines: a `center` or an inline point, with `radiusInM`, `radius`, `radiusMeters` or `radiusInKm`. A value without a usable center or radius throws `OperatorNotValid`.

### Added

- Unit tests.
- AI agent docs in `ai/`, shipped with the package: an `AGENTS.md` overview, rules for entity mapping, querying, units of work, soft delete, and testing, and skills for creating a DAO, geo search, transactions and batches, enabling soft delete, testing, and migrating to 6.x. `npm run check:ai-docs` type-checks their examples.

### Fixed

- `exists` now honors `includeDeleted` instead of always excluding soft deleted documents.
- `count` and `countBy` use Firestore aggregate count queries: `count` was capped at 1000 documents, and `countBy` downloaded every match. `GEO_RADIUS` counts still read the documents, since distance is checked on them.
- `getAll` returns every document instead of the first 1000.
- `FirestoreBatchUnitOfWork.create` uses `batch.create`, so creating an existing document fails the commit instead of overwriting it, as it already did without a unit of work.
- `GEO_RADIUS` searches apply orders, offset and limit to the merged, distance-filtered results. Before, limit and orders were applied to each geohash bound and offset was ignored. The bound queries no longer order by the criteria fields, so they need no composite indexes for them.
- Debug logs no longer pass Firestore references, snapshots, queries, batches, units of work, or entities as context; they log paths, IDs, sizes, and the unit of work's class name. Loggers that clone context, such as the shared kernel's `InMemoryLogger`, threw `DataCloneError` on every DAO call at `debug` level.
- `DataMigrator.migrateFromHardToSoftDelete` reads and commits one page of documents at a time (500 by default, set with a new optional third constructor argument) instead of loading the whole collection into one batch.

## [4.5.0] - 2026-07-02

### Added

- Added `count` method.

## [4.3.0] - 2025-12-30

### Added

- Added a `restore` method.

## [4.2.0] - 2025-12-30

### Added

- Now you can query for deleted records.

## [4.1.0] - 2025-12-30

### Added

- Now there's a deleted_at attribute when using a SOFT delete mode.

## [4.0.1] - 2025-12-21

### Changed

- Updated Shared Kernel version requirement.

## [4.0.0] - 2025-12-06

### Changed

- Now the Shared Kernel package is a peer deep dependency.

## [3.0.2] - 2025-11-14

### Added

- Added `DataMigrator` to update collection to support soft delete method.

## [3.0.1] - 2025-11-14

